file_changes.change:
Add pub(crate) enum LedgerReadFailure { Denied, NotPersistent, Other } and pub(crate) struct LedgerReadError { pub kind: LedgerReadFailure, pub reason: String }, with:
- impl From<String> (kind Other);
- impl std::fmt::Display;
- impl PartialEq<&str> comparing reason.

list_actions and list_actions_with return Result<BTreeMap<String, LedgerRow>, LedgerReadError>. The RPC status maps as:
- zdr_refusal trailer => NotPersistent;
- PermissionDenied or Unauthenticated => Denied;
- else Other(message).
The local errors (no bearer, chunk validation) are Other.

Every existing test compiles and passes unchanged.

New test a_denied_or_zdr_ledger_read_is_told_apart_from_an_unavailable_one.

The dead_code allows on LedgerRow, row_from_state, rows_from_states, list_actions and list_actions_with are removed in step 9.

Step 6: split prepare_resume into consume_for_resume, released_call and build_segment. This is a pure refactor with identical behaviour and refusal order, plus the one warn line continue_replay_refused_ledger_off. ResumedSegment is unchanged.

Step 7: the release pre-reserve reserve_release in the segment's first round, both stages, as approach section I:
- the prereserved skip in phase 2;
- the phase-2 LedgerEntry predicate `ctx.effect_ledger && (class.is_effectful() || release covers)`;
- the hold keeps `class.is_effectful()`;
- the stage-1 Err gives the committed failed text;
- a phase-1-rejected release is reserved then finalized not_run.
Tests listed under step 7.

Step 8: enum RoundSeed { Segment(pb::InferResponse), InPlace(Box<resume::Restored>) }, with only Segment used and identical behaviour.

Step 9 (wiring):
- run_agent_with_route: select_stage, consume, in_place_scope, restore_in_place, the fallback and refusal paths, and the loop_resume_stage log line.
- run_rounds: the InPlace init; the WriterGate `resumed: ctx.release.is_some() && !in_place`; FoldWriter::seeded; the phase-1 seed hooks; save_fence; the in-place error mapping of the pre-reserve.

MockSession knobs (defaults keep today's answers):
- claim_response: Option<Result<pb::ClaimLoopCheckpointResponse, Status>>;
- ledger_rows: Vec<pb::ToolActionState>;
- list_failure: Option<Status>;
- list_calls;
- reserve_already_for: BTreeSet<action_id>.
claim_loop_checkpoint and list_tool_actions push "claim" and "list" to Recorder.order. No current test claims or lists, so no existing order assertion changes; step 0 re-greps this. consume stays out of order and is asserted with consume_calls.len().

The agent tests are listed under step 9.

